{"kind":"symbol","seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/SystemGesture","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/SystemGestureResolver","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/GestureShortcuts","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/ZoomStep","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/PinchUpdate","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/PinchStepper","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/PinchMagnifier","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/MagnifyStep"],"title":"Gestures and zoom","generated":true,"anchor":"Gestures-and-zoom"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/init(chordFingers:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/armed","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/chordFingers","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/silent"],"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/cancelled(_:)","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/down(_:at:time:holding:)","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/moved(_:to:time:)","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/otherTouch()","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/setChordFingers(_:)","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/up(_:at:time:)"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/Gesture","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/Output"],"title":"Enumerations","generated":true,"anchor":"Enumerations"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Three- and four-finger strokes on the glass, for the Mac: which stroke is a gesture, and which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gesture it is. Each input surface feeds one of these with every direct touch, through its stroke"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observer. The counts below say three; with ","type":"text"},{"code":"chordFingers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" 4 read four.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrackpadGestures"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrackpadGestures"}],"externalID":"s:13HeadwireInput16TrackpadGesturesV","roleHeading":"Structure","title":"TrackpadGestures","modules":[{"name":"HeadwireInput"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrackpadGestures"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A stroke runs from its first touch down to its last touch up. It goes "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"silent","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" once three fingers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are down, before any finger has moved "},{"code":"chordTravel","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from where it landed and while no button the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"surface pressed is held (the trackpad’s press-and-hold drag), however slowly they came down and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whatever else rests on the glass. From then until the next stroke’s first touch the surfaces send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing for it, no pointer motion, click, button or scroll (a tap’s action runs after its touch"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has ended, so silence outlasts the last lift). A two-finger scroll that a third finger joins after"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"moving is never silent and goes on as it always did; a stroke that never has three fingers down is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never silent, so one- and two-finger strokes are exactly what they were."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A silent stroke is "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"armed","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", one that can become a gesture, when the three fingers that landed last"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"came down within "},{"code":"chordWindow","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" of each other, before any finger moved "},{"code":"chordTravel","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", with no button"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"held, no touch of the stroke cancelled and at most four fingers down. So a thumb resting on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"glass before neither keeps three fingers from arming nor becomes one of them; three fingers placed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"slowly are silent and decide nothing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The decision comes at the first lift of one of those three (another finger lifting only leaves the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stroke), from their centroid’s net travel since arming, and their spread. A swipe when the centroid","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"travelled ","type":"text"},{"code":"swipeDistance","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (or ","type":"text"},{"code":"flickDistance","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" while moving at ","type":"text"},{"code":"flickSpeed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" over the last","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"flickWindow","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), one axis beats the other by ","type":"text"},{"code":"axisRatio","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the fingers moved together: each of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the three at least ","type":"text"},{"code":"swipeShare","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of the centroid’s way along the swipe, and no other finger that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"moved (","type":"text"},{"code":"chordTravel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or more) that share or more against it. In a pinch or a spread some digit","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"moves against the others, however far the centroid goes (a thumb-led pinch drags it along with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the thumb). Else a pinch or a spread when the mean distance from the centroid changed by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"pinchRatio","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", of the three and every other finger that moved (a thumb pinching with three","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fingers); else nothing. At most one decision per stroke; ","type":"text"},{"code":"fingers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" counts the three and the other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fingers that moved, 4 at most. A fifth finger down leaves the stroke silent and deciding nothing;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"touches the system cancels decide nothing. So a swipe taken back before the lift does nothing, as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on a Mac, and a four-finger stroke that iPadOS takes for itself (its touches cancelled) never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reaches the Mac.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Pure: Foundation and CoreGraphics only, covered by ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackpadGesturesTests","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Deterministic: the same touches give the same outputs. Main thread, as the touches come.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/headwireinput\/trackpadgestures"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://HeadwireInput/documentation/HeadwireInput/MagnifyStep":{"abstract":[{"text":"One event of a magnify gesture on the Mac.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwireinput\/magnifystep","kind":"symbol","title":"MagnifyStep","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MagnifyStep"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/MagnifyStep","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MagnifyStep"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://HeadwireInput/documentation/HeadwireInput/TrackpadGestures/init(chordFingers:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"chordFingers","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwireinput\/trackpadgestures\/init(chordfingers:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a recogniser whose strokes go silent and arm at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chordFingers"},{"type":"text","text":" fingers, 3 or 4."}],"role":"symbol","title":"init(chordFingers:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/init(chordFingers:)","type":"topic"},"doc://HeadwireInput/documentation/HeadwireInput/TrackpadGestures/moved(_:to:time:)":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A finger moves."}],"title":"moved(_:to:time:)","url":"\/documentation\/headwireinput\/trackpadgestures\/moved(_:to:time:)","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/moved(_:to:time:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"moved","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"to"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CGPoint","preciseIdentifier":"c:@S@CGPoint","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"text":"time","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"TimeInterval","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@NSTimeInterval","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}]},"doc://HeadwireInput/documentation/HeadwireInput/TrackpadGestures/otherTouch()":{"type":"topic","title":"otherTouch()","abstract":[{"text":"A touch that is not a finger (a Pencil, the iPad’s own trackpad or mouse) lands. It is never","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"part of a stroke, but with no finger down it starts something new: the last stroke’s silence"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ends, so a Pencil on the portrait trackpad right after a gesture is not ignored.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwireinput\/trackpadgestures\/othertouch()","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput\/TrackpadGestures\/otherTouch()","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"otherTouch"},{"kind":"tex